0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 703.0 Tm (Why not just make the model refuse?) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 684.5 Tm (A careful model helps but can still be tricked, and then nothing stops it. Deterministic policy) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 670.0 Tm (is the part that does not depend on the model's judgement.) Tj ET
0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 637.0 Tm (What does the scanner add if the gateway decides?) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 618.5 Tm (An extra signal that can only escalate a decision to human approval. If it is fooled or crashes,) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 604.0 Tm (the gateway still holds.) Tj ET
0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 571.0 Tm (How is an approval tied to one action?) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 552.5 Tm (The token is the request id plus HMAC-SHA256 over request id, session, action hash and expiry.) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 538.0 Tm (The action hash covers the session, tool and canonical arguments. Redeeming checks the signature) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 523.5 Tm (in constant time, status, expiry, session and an exact hash match; any change triggers A008.) Tj ET
0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 490.5 Tm (Why do 10% of held-out attacks still succeed?) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 472.0 Tm (One case rewrites an already-allowed reply to an approved recipient. Every permission check) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 457.5 Tm (passes by design; the person approving the send is the defence there.) Tj ET
0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 424.5 Tm (How do you know the rules were not tuned to the test?) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 406.0 Tm (The held-out attacks were written after the rules were frozen, and test_freeze.py fails if the) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 391.5 Tm (policy, engine or scanner change.) Tj ET
0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 358.5 Tm (How do you know the tests catch security bugs?) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 340.0 Tm (Mutation testing injects 26 security bugs one at a time; each one makes at least one test fail.) Tj ET
0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 307.0 Tm (The data is synthetic. What do the results mean?) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 288.5 Tm (The attack benchmark is synthetic by design so every case is safe and labelled; the gateway) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 274.0 Tm (logic is the same on real traffic. The classifier was also tested on 56,711 real emails.) Tj ET
0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 241.0 Tm (Is the classifier overfitted?) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 222.5 Tm (Synthetic results use grouped cross-validation; real results use a separate 30% test set, with) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 208.0 Tm (duplicates removed, Enron words masked, L2 regularisation and min_df=2.) Tj ET
0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 175.0 Tm (Did you train an LLM?) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 156.5 Tm (No. Only the email classifier is trained. The gateway is rules, so no data can teach it to) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 142.0 Tm (relax.) Tj ET
0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 109.0 Tm (How fast is it?) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 90.5 Tm (About 0.08 ms per decision, including the audit write.) Tj ET

endstream
