0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 703.0 Tm (Does it work with other models?) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 684.5 Tm (Yes. The gateway is model-agnostic; llm_client.py talks to any OpenAI-compatible API or a local) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 670.0 Tm (Ollama model.) Tj ET
0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 637.0 Tm (Is the dashboard secure?) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 618.5 Tm (It is a localhost demo server with a strict Content-Security-Policy, security headers, size) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 604.0 Tm (limits, JSON-only requests and validated inputs. It has no user accounts, so it should not be) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 589.5 Tm (exposed to the internet.) Tj ET
0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 556.5 Tm (Has this been built before?) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 538.0 Tm (The idea exists in research and in some products. Aegis contributes a working, tested,) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 523.5 Tm (explainable implementation with an honest benchmark, not a new theory.) Tj ET
0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 490.5 Tm (What would you build next?) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 472.0 Tm (An MCP gateway, so Aegis protects real AI apps without changing them.) Tj ET
0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 439.0 Tm (Why use synthetic data if you have real Kaggle emails?) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 420.5 Tm (They answer different questions. Real emails test the classifier, and that is where its 97.7%) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 406.0 Tm (and 99.7% come from. The attack benchmark needs tasks, files, tools and attacker goals, which an) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 391.5 Tm (email dataset does not have, and real attacks on a real mailbox would be unsafe.) Tj ET
0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 358.5 Tm (Why no web framework?) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 340.0 Tm (Fewer dependencies mean fewer vulnerabilities and no install step, and the whole server can be) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 325.5 Tm (read in one sitting. For a security tool, small and auditable is the point.) Tj ET
0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 292.5 Tm (What does CI run, and why is mutation testing not in it?) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 274.0 Tm (Lint, type checks and all tests on four Python versions for every change. Mutation testing runs) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 259.5 Tm (the full suite 26 times, which is too slow per change, so it is run before releases.) Tj ET
0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 226.5 Tm (What is a TaskGrant?) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 208.0 Tm (The permissions for one task: allowed tools, emails, files, recipients, maximum sensitivity and) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 193.5 Tm (expiry. It is created only from the user's request \(aegis/agent/tasks.py\), never from content) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 179.0 Tm (the agent reads.) Tj ET
0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 146.0 Tm (What is egress control?) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 127.5 Tm (Rules on where data may go. The session tracks the most sensitive data it has read; confidential) Tj ET
0.13 0.13 0.13 rg BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 113.0 Tm (data may never be sent outside the organisation, however the agent rewords it.) Tj ET
0.12 0.23 0.37 rg BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.0 80.0 Tm (How is the audit log tamper-evident?) Tj ET

